   "vs_population": "writeup 464 population (16-dim bundle, class_sparing) capitalized dissociation = +0.0059. This leaf's own bundle gives +0.0061, nominally 0.0002 above population, but the row-level 95% bootstrap CI [-0.0198,+0.0379] comfortably contains both the population value AND zero (and even negative values). The apparent excess is noise, not a reproducible leaf-specific effect.",
   "random_control": "Rank-matched random orthonormal subspace in the same component (a7, rank24), 3 seeds, scored on the same fresh rows/class: dissociation -0.0031/+0.0034/+0.0096. One random seed alone (+0.0096) exceeds the leaf's own real-bundle effect (+0.0061) -- the control is NOT clean, the real effect is statistically indistinguishable from same-rank random ablation in this component.",
   "objection": "The claimed excess over population (0.0002) is two orders of magnitude smaller than both the bootstrap CI half-width (~0.029) and the random-control spread (~0.013 across just 3 seeds) -- there is no basis to call this leaf-specific. Independently of the numbers, BILIN18_CONNECTION.md 453/455/456/462/463 already show this punctuation-spared/content-damaged dissociation is a generic property reproduced by ablating many unrelated components in this model (a frequency account and a prediction-confidence account were both tested and refuted, and only 462 established a genuinely leaf-agnostic version survives at all). A CONFIRM here would misattribute a well-documented general bias to a7's specific machinery, which is especially unsupported given the mechanism gate already failed (no enriched writer into a7)."
